<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Function Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01392</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Function Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>eeadf469-35b2-44c0-8397-57265acb07a1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">For questions 1 - 3, the graph shows the population of beavers in a forest for different numbers of years after 1995. The beaver population is growing exponentially.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">

        <media alt="A scatter plot showing the number of beavers over 5 years. Red points show increases: (1,100), (2,200), (3,400), (4,800). The y-axis is number of beavers and the x-axis is time in years.">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_10_09_01.svg"/>
        </media>

      </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003"> Explain why we can think of the beaver population as a function of time in years.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00006"> The number of beavers depends on time in years. In any given year, there is a particular number of beavers in the forest.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007"> What is the meaning of the point labeled <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>Q</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> in this context?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00010"> The point <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>Q</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> indicates that 3.5 years after 1995, the beaver population was about 550.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00011"> Write an equation using function notation to represent this situation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00014">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> where <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>t</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is years after 1995 and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>t</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> is the beaver population at that time.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->

      <exercise id="_0c20dc9a-915d-4066-ab59-64b5717b29be" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Which equation is most appropriate for modeling this data?</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="6">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
<m:math>
              <m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>                  </entry>
                  <entry>1</entry>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>3</entry>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><m:math>
              <m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>14</entry>
                  <entry>26</entry>
                  <entry>74</entry>
                  <entry>266</entry>
                  <entry>1034</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          <caption>This table displays corresponding numerical values for variables x and y across five data points, suggesting a functional relationship between them.</caption></table><list list-type="enumerated" number-style="lower-alpha" id="list-00001">          
          <item><para id="para-00004"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para></item>
          <item><para id="para-00008"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para></item>
          <item><para id="para-00012"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para></item>
          <item><para id="para-00017"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para></item>
            </list>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00021"><m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

    </section>
  </content>
</document>
